'''Avestan geography''' is the investigation of place names in the [[Avesta]] and the attempt to connect them to real-world geographical sites.{{Sfn|Gnoli|2011}}{{Sfn|Eilers|1980}} It is connected to but different from the [[Karshvar|cosmogony]] expressed in the Avesta, where place names primarily refer to [[Persian mythology|mythical events]] or a [[Zoroastrian cosmology|cosmological order]].{{Sfn|Kreyenbroek|2011}}

Identifying such connections is important for localizing the [[Avestan period|people of the Avesta]] and is therefore crucial for understanding the early history of [[Zoroastrianism]] and the [[Arya (Iran)|Iranians]].{{Sfn|Grenet|2015}}{{Sfn|Witzel|2013}}{{Sfn|Skjaervø|1995|loc=p. 158 "In view of the dearth of historical sources it is of paramount importance that one should evaluate the evidence of the Avesta, the holy book of the Zoroastrians, parts at least of which antedate the Old Persian inscriptions by several centuries."}} Sources for such geographical references are exclusively found in the younger [[Avestan]] portion of the text, in particular in the [[Vendidad]] and several of the [[Yasht]]s. The identification of these Avestan places with real locations is often supported by comparisons with references made in later Iranian sources.{{Sfn|Vogelsang|2000|loc=p. 50 "While many of the names in the list can be compared with names that occur in other sources (e.g. the Achaemenid inscriptions and classical sources), others remain to be convincingly identified."}} 

A major challenge to establish these connections is the fact that the Iranian people often used the same name for different places.{{sfn|Yarshater|1983|loc=p. 352: "[L]ike most migrants, the early Iranians seem to have applied old names to new places"}} As a result, not all Avestan place names can be identified with certainty with present-day locations and therefore remain subject to debate. Modern scholarship, however, agrees that the place names in the Avesta are concentrated in the eastern regions of [[Greater Iran]] up to the [[Ancient India|Indo]]-[[Ancient Iran|Iranian]] border.{{Sfn|Gnoli|2011}}

